<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Auxiliary Lemmas</h2>

<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem 12 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fan et al. (2021)</a></cite>)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Markov chain on the finite state space <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>
with transition matrix <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and initial distribution <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}\sim p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}\sim p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume the Markov chain induced by <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is ergodic
with stationary distribution <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\pi}^{*}=\operatorname{diag}(\mu_{\pi})^{-1}P_{\pi}^{\top}\operatorname{diag}(\mu_{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\pi}^{*}=\operatorname{diag}(\mu_{\pi})^{-1}P_{\pi}^{\top}\operatorname{diag}(\mu_{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math>
denote the time reversal of <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the
additive reversiblization <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\pi}\doteq(P_{\pi}+P_{\pi}^{*})/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\pi}\doteq(P_{\pi}+P_{\pi}^{*})/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the second-largest eigenvalue of <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>,
so that <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\lambda_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\lambda_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the right spectral gap.
Then for any function <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon\mathcal{S}\to[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon\mathcal{S}\to[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\!\bigg(\,\bigg|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}f(S_{k})-\mu_{\pi}(f)\bigg|&gt;\epsilon\,\bigg)\leq\frac{2}{\mu_{\min}}\,\exp\!\bigg(\!-\frac{1-\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}{1+\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}\cdot\frac{2n\epsilon^{2}}{(b-a)^{2}}\bigg)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\bigg(\,\bigg|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}f(S_{k})-\mu_{\pi}(f)\bigg|&gt;\epsilon\,\bigg)\leq\frac{2}{\mu_{\min}}\,\exp\!\bigg(\!-\frac{1-\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}{1+\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}\cdot\frac{2n\epsilon^{2}}{(b-a)^{2}}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\min}\doteq\min_{s\in\mathcal{S}}\mu_{\pi}(s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\min}\doteq\min_{s\in\mathcal{S}}\mu_{\pi}(s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any finite irreducible aperiodic chain,
<math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite reversible irreducible chain,
so <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{r}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{r}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and the bound is nontrivial.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This is a special case of Theorem 12 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fan et al. (2021)</a></cite>
with burn-in length <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and integrability exponent <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,
so that the prefactor becomes
<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\nu,0,\infty)=\lVert p_{0}/\mu_{\pi}\rVert_{\infty}\leq 1/\mu_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\nu,0,\infty)=\lVert p_{0}/\mu_{\pi}\rVert_{\infty}\leq 1/\mu_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Proposition A.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ortega and Rheinboldt (2000)</a></cite>)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be continuously differentiable.
Then for any <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w,w^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w,w^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f(w)-f(w^{\prime})\|_{\infty}\;\leq\;\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\|Df(w+t(w^{\prime}-w))\|_{\infty}\;\|w-w^{\prime}\|_{\infty}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f(w)-f(w^{\prime})\|_{\infty}\;\leq\;\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\|Df(w+t(w^{\prime}-w))\|_{\infty}\;\|w-w^{\prime}\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Df(z)\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Df(z)\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Jacobian of <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove by induction that, for every layer <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the prompt admits the form</span></p>
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l}\doteq\begin{bmatrix}x_{0}&amp;x_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;x_{n-1}&amp;x_{n}\\
R_{1}&amp;R_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;R_{n}&amp;0\\
\gamma v_{l}(S_{1})&amp;\gamma v_{l}(S_{2})&amp;\cdots&amp;\gamma v_{l}(S_{n})&amp;0\\
v_{l}(S_{0})&amp;v_{l}(S_{1})&amp;\cdots&amp;v_{l}(S_{n-1})&amp;v_{l}(S_{n})\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l}\doteq\begin{bmatrix}x_{0}&amp;x_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;x_{n-1}&amp;x_{n}\\
R_{1}&amp;R_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;R_{n}&amp;0\\
\gamma v_{l}(S_{1})&amp;\gamma v_{l}(S_{2})&amp;\cdots&amp;\gamma v_{l}(S_{n})&amp;0\\
v_{l}(S_{0})&amp;v_{l}(S_{1})&amp;\cdots&amp;v_{l}(S_{n-1})&amp;v_{l}(S_{n})\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">This holds at <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=0</annotation></semantics></math> by the definition of <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In Weighted softmax TD. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now fix any <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and assume that <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies (<a href="#A2.E37" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>).
We derive the layer update induced by <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{l},A_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{l},A_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E15" title="In Current-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
Since <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}=\operatorname{diag}(I_{d},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}=\operatorname{diag}(I_{d},0)</annotation></semantics></math>, the score matrix depends only on the first <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> rows of <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under (<a href="#A2.E37" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>), the first <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> entries of the <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-th column of <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> equal <math id="A2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{l}^{\top}A_{l}Z_{l})[i,j]=\langle x_{i-1},x_{j-1}\rangle,\quad i,j=1,\dots,n+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{l}^{\top}A_{l}Z_{l})[i,j]=\langle x_{i-1},x_{j-1}\rangle,\quad i,j=1,\dots,n+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore the attention matrix <math id="A2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{K}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{K}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is layer-invariant (denoted as <math id="A2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{K}</annotation></semantics></math>).
By softmax weights <math id="A2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E12" title="In Weighted softmax TD. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), for every <math id="A2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{K}[k,j+1]=\begin{cases}K(S_{k-1},S_{j}),&amp;k=1,\dots,n,\\
0,&amp;k=n+1\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{K}[k,j+1]=\begin{cases}K(S_{k-1},S_{j}),&amp;k=1,\dots,n,\\
0,&amp;k=n+1\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, consider the current-value head.
For each context column <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(V_{l}Z_{l})[d+3,k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(V_{l}Z_{l})[d+3,k]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{1\times d}&amp;1&amp;1&amp;-1\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}x_{k-1}\\
R_{k}\\
\gamma v_{l}(S_{k})\\
v_{l}(S_{k-1})\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{1\times d}&amp;1&amp;1&amp;-1\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}x_{k-1}\\
R_{k}\\
\gamma v_{l}(S_{k})\\
v_{l}(S_{k-1})\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=R_{k}+\gamma v_{l}(S_{k})-v_{l}(S_{k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=R_{k}+\gamma v_{l}(S_{k})-v_{l}(S_{k-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta_{k}^{(l)}\quad\text{(By \eqref{eq:tderror})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mtext>(By (</mtext><mtext><a href="#S3.E11" title="In Weighted softmax TD. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a></mtext><mtext>))</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta_{k}^{(l)}\quad\text{(By \eqref{eq:tderror})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the last column,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{l}Z_{l})[d+3,n+1]=\begin{bmatrix}0_{1\times d}&amp;1&amp;1&amp;-1\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}x_{n}\\
0\\
0\\
v_{l}(S_{n})\end{bmatrix}=-v_{l}(S_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{l}Z_{l})[d+3,n+1]=\begin{bmatrix}0_{1\times d}&amp;1&amp;1&amp;-1\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}x_{n}\\
0\\
0\\
v_{l}(S_{n})\end{bmatrix}=-v_{l}(S_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\delta}^{(l)}\doteq[\delta_{1}^{(l)},\dots,\delta_{n}^{(l)},-v_{l}(S_{n})],\qquad\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\doteq[\delta_{1}^{(l)},\dots,\delta_{n}^{(l)},0]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\delta}^{(l)}\doteq[\delta_{1}^{(l)},\dots,\delta_{n}^{(l)},-v_{l}(S_{n})],\qquad\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\doteq[\delta_{1}^{(l)},\dots,\delta_{n}^{(l)},0].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since the last row of <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is zero, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}=\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}=\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta Z_{l}[d+3,:]=\big(V_{l}Z_{l}\,\mathrm{softmax}(Z_{l}^{\top}A_{l}Z_{l})\big)[d+3,:]=\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta Z_{l}[d+3,:]=\big(V_{l}Z_{l}\,\mathrm{softmax}(Z_{l}^{\top}A_{l}Z_{l})\big)[d+3,:]=\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the target-value head, (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta Z_{l}[d+2,:]=\gamma\,\big(V_{l}Z_{l}\,\mathrm{softmax}(Z_{l}^{\top}A_{l}Z_{l})\Pi\big)[d+3,:]=\gamma\,\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}\Pi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi><msup><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta Z_{l}[d+2,:]=\gamma\,\big(V_{l}Z_{l}\,\mathrm{softmax}(Z_{l}^{\top}A_{l}Z_{l})\Pi\big)[d+3,:]=\gamma\,\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}\Pi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now read out the last column.
Using (<a href="#S3.E19" title="In Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E43" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{l+1}(S_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{l+1}(S_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Z_{l+1}[d+3,n+1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Z_{l+1}[d+3,n+1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Z_{l}[d+3,n+1]+\Delta Z_{l}[d+3,n+1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Z_{l}[d+3,n+1]+\Delta Z_{l}[d+3,n+1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=v_{l}(S_{n})+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\delta_{k}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}[k,n+1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=v_{l}(S_{n})+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\delta_{k}^{(l)}\widetilde{K}[k,n+1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=v_{l}(S_{n})+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\delta_{k}^{(l)}K(S_{k-1},S_{n})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=v_{l}(S_{n})+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\delta_{k}^{(l)}K(S_{k-1},S_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is exactly (<a href="#S3.E20" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to verify that <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l+1}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the form in (<a href="#A2.E37" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>).
By construction, only rows <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+3</annotation></semantics></math> are modified, so the first <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1</annotation></semantics></math> rows remain unchanged.
Moreover, for every <math id="A2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, using (<a href="#A2.E43" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l+1}[d+3,j+1]=v_{l}(S_{j})+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\delta_{k}^{(l)}K(S_{k-1},S_{j})=v_{l+1}(S_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l+1}[d+3,j+1]=v_{l}(S_{j})+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\delta_{k}^{(l)}K(S_{k-1},S_{j})=v_{l+1}(S_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus the last row stores the synchronous weighted softmax TD updates for all trajectory states.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, right multiplication by <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> shifts columns to the left.
Hence for every <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, using (<a href="#A2.E44" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{l+1}[d+2,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{l+1}[d+2,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Z_{l}[d+2,j]+\gamma(\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K})_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Z_{l}[d+2,j]+\gamma(\boldsymbol{\delta}^{(l)}\widetilde{K})_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\gamma v_{l}(S_{j})+\gamma\big(v_{l+1}(S_{j})-v_{l}(S_{j})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\gamma v_{l}(S_{j})+\gamma\big(v_{l+1}(S_{j})-v_{l}(S_{j})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\gamma v_{l+1}(S_{j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\gamma v_{l+1}(S_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Also, <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l+1}[d+2,n+1]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l+1}[d+2,n+1]=0</annotation></semantics></math> because the last column of <math id="A2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> is zero.
Therefore <math id="A2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l+1}</annotation></semantics></math> again satisfies (<a href="#A2.E37" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>), completing the induction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs in Section <span id="A3.2" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S4" title="4 Dual-Head Attention = Single-Head Attention + Temporal Shift Module ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span></h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <span id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_text"><a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 4 Dual-Head Attention = Single-Head Attention + Temporal Shift Module ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">From (<a href="#A2.E37" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>), <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies that <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z_{l}[d+2,:]=\gamma Z_{l}[d+3,:]\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l}[d+2,:]=\gamma Z_{l}[d+3,:]\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Using this invariant, by (<a href="#S4.E21" title="In 4 Dual-Head Attention = Single-Head Attention + Temporal Shift Module ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l+\frac{1}{2}}=Z_{l}+\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+3)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l+\frac{1}{2}}=Z_{l}+\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+3)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+3)}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In Current-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).
By (<a href="#S4.E23" title="In 4 Dual-Head Attention = Single-Head Attention + Temporal Shift Module ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), the TSM step leaves the first <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d+1)</annotation></semantics></math> rows unchanged and,
for every column <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(Z_{l+1})_{d+3,k}=(Z_{l+\frac{1}{2}})_{d+3,k},\qquad(Z_{l+1})_{d+2,:}=\gamma(Z_{l+\frac{1}{2}})_{d+3,:}\Pi," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{l+1})_{d+3,k}=(Z_{l+\frac{1}{2}})_{d+3,k},\qquad(Z_{l+1})_{d+2,:}=\gamma(Z_{l+\frac{1}{2}})_{d+3,:}\Pi,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>).
Therefore <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l+1}=Z_{l+\frac{1}{2}}+\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l+1}=Z_{l+\frac{1}{2}}+\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+2)}</annotation></semantics></math>
coincides with (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>).
Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l+1}=Z_{l}+\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+3)}+\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+2)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l+1}=Z_{l}+\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+3)}+\Delta Z_{l}^{(d+2)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is exactly (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>). Hence the dual-head update equals the
single-head+TSM update in (<a href="#S4.E23" title="In 4 Dual-Head Attention = Single-Head Attention + Temporal Shift Module ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs of Section <span id="A4.2" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S5" title="5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></span></h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <span id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_text"><a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Recall <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{M}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S5.E24" title="In 5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) and <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S5.E27" title="In 5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>).
For any <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist constants
<math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},1},C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},1},C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
such that with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{M}_{n}-M_{\pi}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},1}\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},2}/\delta)}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{M}_{n}-M_{\pi}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},1}\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},2}/\delta)}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the empirical state frequency</span></p>
<table id="A4.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{n}(s)\doteq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\mathbbm{1}\{S_{k-1}=s\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≐</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{n}(s)\doteq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\mathbbm{1}\{S_{k-1}=s\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Theorem 12 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix A Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f=\mathbbm{1}\{\cdot=s\}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\mathbbm{1}\{\cdot=s\}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>
and a union bound over <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\!\Big(\|\hat{\mu}_{n}-\mu_{\pi}\|_{\infty}&gt;\epsilon\Big)\;\leq\;\frac{2|\mathcal{S}|}{\mu_{\min}}\exp\!\bigg(\!-\frac{1-\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}{1+\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}\cdot 2n\epsilon^{2}\bigg)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\Big(\|\hat{\mu}_{n}-\mu_{\pi}\|_{\infty}&gt;\epsilon\Big)\;\leq\;\frac{2|\mathcal{S}|}{\mu_{\min}}\exp\!\bigg(\!-\frac{1-\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}{1+\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}\cdot 2n\epsilon^{2}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Setting the right-hand side equal to <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and solving for <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> yields that
with probability at least <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\mu}_{n}-\mu_{\pi}\|_{\infty}\leq\sqrt{\frac{1+\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}{2(1-\max\{\lambda_{r},0\})}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(2|\fS|/(\mu_{\min}\,\delta))}{n}}\doteq C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},3}\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},4}/\delta)}{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>≐</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\mu}_{n}-\mu_{\pi}\|_{\infty}\leq\sqrt{\frac{1+\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}{2(1-\max\{\lambda_{r},0\})}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(2|\fS|/(\mu_{\min}\,\delta))}{n}}\doteq C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},3}\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},4}/\delta)}{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">where
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},3}\doteq\sqrt{\frac{1+\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}{2(1-\max\{\lambda_{r},0\})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},3}\doteq\sqrt{\frac{1+\max\{\lambda_{r},0\}}{2(1-\max\{\lambda_{r},0\})}}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},4}\doteq\frac{2|\mathcal{S}|}{\mu_{\min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ref{lem:concentration-Mn},4}\doteq\frac{2|\mathcal{S}|}{\mu_{\min}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to transfer (<a href="#A4.E48" title="In Proof. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) to <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{M}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{M}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By expanding (<a href="#S5.E24" title="In 5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) with (<a href="#A4.E46" title="In Proof. ‣ D.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{M}_{n}(s,s^{\prime})=\frac{\hat{\mu}_{n}(s^{\prime})\,\exp(\langle x(s), x(s') \rangle)}{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{S}}\hat{\mu}_{n}(u)\,\exp(\langle x(s), x(u) \rangle)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{M}_{n}(s,s^{\prime})=\frac{\hat{\mu}_{n}(s^{\prime})\,\exp(\langle x(s), x(s') \rangle)}{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{S}}\hat{\mu}_{n}(u)\,\exp(\langle x(s), x(u) \rangle)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
