</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to control <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\norm{X_L}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\norm{X_L}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> deterministically. Let <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}\doteq I-M_{n}^{c}+\gamma\widehat{P}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}\doteq I-M_{n}^{c}+\gamma\widehat{P}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{n}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{P}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{P}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are nonnegative row-stochastic, <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\norm{G_n}_{\infty}\leq 2+\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\norm{G_n}_{\infty}\leq 2+\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this to the recursion (<a href="#S5.E25" title="In 5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) with <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\norm{v_{l+1}}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\norm{v_{l+1}}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E98.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(2+\gamma)\norm{v_l}_{\infty}+C_{R}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\norm{v_L}_{\infty}\leq\frac{C_{R}\quantity((2+\gamma)^L-1)}{1+\gamma}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(2+\gamma)\norm{v_l}_{\infty}+C_{R}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\norm{v_L}_{\infty}\leq\frac{C_{R}\quantity((2+\gamma)^L-1)}{1+\gamma},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\absolutevalue{\bar\delta_L(\theta_*)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\absolutevalue{\bar\delta_L(\theta_*)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E99.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{R}+(1+\gamma)\norm{v_L}_{\infty}\leq C_{R}(2+\gamma)^{L}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{R}+(1+\gamma)\norm{v_L}_{\infty}\leq C_{R}(2+\gamma)^{L}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the gradient, from the proof of Lemma <span id="A5.SS4.p5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#Thmlemma10" title="Lemma 10. ‣ E.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix E Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a></span> there exists a constant <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A5.E100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\norm{g_l}_{\infty}\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}(C_{R}+(1+\gamma)\norm{v_l}_{\infty})\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}C_{R}(2+\gamma)^{l}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\norm{g_l}_{\infty}\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}(C_{R}+(1+\gamma)\norm{v_l}_{\infty})\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}C_{R}(2+\gamma)^{l}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Unrolling <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}v_{l+1}=G_{n}\nabla_{\theta}v_{l}+g_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}v_{l+1}=G_{n}\nabla_{\theta}v_{l}+g_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}v_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}v_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\norm{\nabla_\theta v_L}_{\infty}\leq\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}(2+\gamma)^{L-1-l}\norm{g_l}_{\infty}\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}C_{R}\,L(2+\gamma)^{L-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\norm{\nabla_\theta v_L}_{\infty}\leq\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}(2+\gamma)^{L-1-l}\norm{g_l}_{\infty}\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}C_{R}\,L(2+\gamma)^{L-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A5.E99" title="In Proof. ‣ E.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">99</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E101" title="In Proof. ‣ E.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">101</span></a>), and defining <math id="A5.SS4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},10}\doteq D_{\theta}\,C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}\,C_{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},10}\doteq D_{\theta}\,C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},9}\,C_{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\norm{X_L}_{1}\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},10}\,L(2+\gamma)^{2L}\qquad\text{for every trajectory.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>for every trajectory.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\norm{X_L}_{1}\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},10}\,L(2+\gamma)^{2L}\qquad\text{for every trajectory.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting (<a href="#A5.E97" title="In Proof. ‣ E.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">97</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E102" title="In Proof. ‣ E.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">102</span></a>) into (<a href="#A5.E94" title="In Proof. ‣ E.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Proofs of Section ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">94</span></a>) and setting <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=1/n</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{L}(\theta_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{L}(\theta_{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},8}\quantity[
(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^L
+
\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}
]\quantity[
1+
\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}
]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S5.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 5.1. ‣ 5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},8}\quantity[
(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^L
+
\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}
]\quantity[
1+
\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}
]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},10}\frac{L(2+\gamma)^{2L}}{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},10}\frac{L(2+\gamma)^{2L}}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},11}\doteq 1+\log C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},5}/\log 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},11}\doteq 1+\log C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},5}/\log 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},5}\geq e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},5}\geq e</annotation></semantics></math>, for every <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},11}\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},11}\log n</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> so that for every <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},4}\log n\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}\leq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},4}\log n\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a+b)(1+b)\leq a+3b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a+b)(1+b)\leq a+3b</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\quantity[
(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^L
+
\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}
]\quantity[
1+
\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}
]\leq(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^{L}+3\sqrt{C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},11}}\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S5.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 5.1. ‣ 5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S5.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 5.1. ‣ 5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quantity[
(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^L
+
\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}
]\quantity[
1+
\sqrt{\frac{\log(C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},5}n)}{n}}
]\leq(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^{L}+3\sqrt{C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},11}}\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, with</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},2}\doteq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},8}\max\quantity(1,\,3\sqrt{C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},11}}),\qquad C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},3}\doteq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},10}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},2}\doteq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},8}\max\quantity(1,\,3\sqrt{C_{\text{Thm}\tref{thm:emergence},11}}),\qquad C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},3}\doteq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},10},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain (<a href="#S6.E33" title="In Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>): for all <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{L}(\theta_{*})\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},2}\quantity[
(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^L
+
\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}
]+C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},3}\frac{L(2+\gamma)^{2L}}{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S5.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 5.1. ‣ 5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{L}(\theta_{*})\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},2}\quantity[
(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^L
+
\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}
]+C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},3}\frac{L(2+\gamma)^{2L}}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, for every fixed <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup_{n\to\infty}J_{L}(\theta_{*})\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},2}(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>Thm</mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S5.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 5.1. ‣ 5 Inference-Time Convergence ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup_{n\to\infty}J_{L}(\theta_{*})\leq C_{\text{Thm}\text{\ref{thm:emergence}},2}(1-C_{\ref{ass:diagonal-margin}})^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, and taking <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{L\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty}J_{L}(\theta_{*})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{L\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty}J_{L}(\theta_{*})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Additional Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Multi-task TD</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pseudocode of multi-task TD is provided in Algorithm 1.
Notably, <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{TF}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>TF</mtext><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{TF}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.1 Transformers and Softmax Self-Attention ‣ 2 Background ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).
The training update is semi-gradient TD, where
the bootstrap target <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0}^{\prime};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>TF</mtext><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0}^{\prime};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is held fixed,
so the single-sample update direction is <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mtext>TF</mtext><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is a stochastic estimate of the expected update field
in the NEU objective (<a href="#S6.E31" title="In 6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To accelerate training in some settings, we introduce a scalar diagonal mixing coefficient <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> at the attention level.
Let <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{l}\doteq Z_{l}^{\top}A_{l}Z_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{l}\doteq Z_{l}^{\top}A_{l}Z_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and fix a softmax temperature <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
At training step <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> the kernel is</p>
<table id="A6.E104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E104.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{K}[i,j](\rho_{t})\doteq(1-\rho_{t})\cdot\frac{\exp(L_{l,ij}/\tau)}{\sum_{m=0}^{n-1}\exp(L_{l,mj}/\tau)}+\rho_{t}\cdot\mathbbm{1}\{i=j\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{K}[i,j](\rho_{t})\doteq(1-\rho_{t})\cdot\frac{\exp(L_{l,ij}/\tau)}{\sum_{m=0}^{n-1}\exp(L_{l,mj}/\tau)}+\rho_{t}\cdot\mathbbm{1}\{i=j\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Importantly, all results in Section <span id="A6.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S8" title="8 Experiments ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></span> are trained with <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>  Multi-Task Temporal Difference Learning with softmax Softmax Transformer</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span>
context length <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>,
MRP number of states <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>,
MRP sample length <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>,
number of training tasks <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>,
learning rate <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>,
discount factor <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>,
diagonal mixing <math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
softmax temperature <math id="alg1.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>,
transformer parameters <math id="alg1.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\doteq\quantity(V, A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\doteq\quantity(V, A)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{0},p,r,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{0},p,r,x)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{task}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>task</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{task}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{0},R_{1},S_{1},R_{2},\dots,S_{H},R_{H+1},S_{H+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{0},R_{1},S_{1},R_{2},\dots,S_{H},R_{H+1},S_{H+1})</annotation></semantics></math> from the MRP <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{0},p,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{0},p,r)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,\dots,H-n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,\dots,H-n-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
               // Build two consecutive prompt windows

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
               // Query uses the state after the last context transition: <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{q}\doteq x_{t+n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>≐</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{q}\doteq x_{t+n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{q}^{\prime}\doteq x_{t+n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≐</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{q}^{\prime}\doteq x_{t+n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{0}\leftarrow\matrixquantity[\lx@physics@matrix x_{t} &amp; \cdots&amp; x_{t+n-1} &amp; x_{q} \\
R_{t+1} &amp; \cdots&amp; R_{t+n} &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; \cdots&amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; \cdots&amp; 0 &amp; 0\endlx@physics@matrix]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{0}\leftarrow\matrixquantity[\lx@physics@matrix x_{t} &amp; \cdots&amp; x_{t+n-1} &amp; x_{q} \\
R_{t+1} &amp; \cdots&amp; R_{t+n} &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; \cdots&amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; \cdots&amp; 0 &amp; 0\endlx@physics@matrix]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{0}^{\prime}\leftarrow\matrixquantity[\lx@physics@matrix x_{t+1} &amp; \cdots&amp; x_{t+n} &amp; x_{q}' \\
R_{t+2} &amp; \cdots&amp; R_{t+n+1} &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; \cdots&amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; \cdots&amp; 0 &amp; 0\endlx@physics@matrix]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{0}^{\prime}\leftarrow\matrixquantity[\lx@physics@matrix x_{t+1} &amp; \cdots&amp; x_{t+n} &amp; x_{q}' \\
R_{t+2} &amp; \cdots&amp; R_{t+n+1} &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; \cdots&amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; \cdots&amp; 0 &amp; 0\endlx@physics@matrix]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
               // semi-gradient TD

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}\leftarrow R_{t+n+1}+\gamma\,\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0}^{\prime};\theta)-\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>TF</mtext><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>TF</mtext><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}\leftarrow R_{t+n+1}+\gamma\,\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0}^{\prime};\theta)-\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta+\eta\delta_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mtext>TF</mtext><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta+\eta\delta_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\text{TF}_{L}(Z_{0};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Minimal Sparse Parameterization</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a minimal sparse parameterization that prevents the block from overwriting features or rewards,
while leaving the structured computation to be learned from data.
Notably, this sparsification is strictly lighter than the sparse parameter space used in Section <span id="A6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S6" title="6 Emergence of Softmax ICTD under Reinforcement Pretraining ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></span>.
The masks below are fixed throughout training, and all trainable entries are initialized by Xavier normal initialization with gain <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mask on <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(n+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(n+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#A2.E37" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>).
We enforce a fixed sparsity pattern via an elementwise mask
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{mask}}\in\{0,1\}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>mask</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{mask}}\in\{0,1\}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}</annotation></semantics></math> and parameterize</p>
<table id="A6.E105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{0}=\widetilde{V}\odot V_{\mathrm{mask}},\qquad\widetilde{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>mask</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{0}=\widetilde{V}\odot V_{\mathrm{mask}},\qquad\widetilde{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The mask is fixed throughout training and only allows the last two rows to be nonzero:</p>
<table id="A6.E106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{mask}}=\begin{bmatrix}0_{(d+1)\times(d+3)}\\
\mathbbm{1}_{2\times(d+3)}\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>mask</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{mask}}=\begin{bmatrix}0_{(d+1)\times(d+3)}\\
\mathbbm{1}_{2\times(d+3)}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">As a result, the additive update <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{0}Z_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{0}Z_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> modifies only the two value slots of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mask on <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the logits mixing matrix used to form the pre-softmax logits
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{l}^{\top}A_{0}Z_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{l}^{\top}A_{0}Z_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>. We impose the block sparsity via an elementwise mask
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{mask}}\in\{0,1\}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>mask</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{mask}}\in\{0,1\}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}</annotation></semantics></math> and parameterize</p>
<table id="A6.E107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}=\widetilde{A}\odot A_{\mathrm{mask}},\qquad\widetilde{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>mask</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}=\widetilde{A}\odot A_{\mathrm{mask}},\qquad\widetilde{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(d+3)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We split rows and columns into the first <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> feature channels and the last <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> scalar channels, and set the
scalar-to-scalar block to zero by</p>
<table id="A6.E108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{mask}}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbbm{1}_{d\times d}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{d\times 3}\\
\mathbf{0}_{3\times d}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{3\times 3}\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>mask</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{mask}}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbbm{1}_{d\times d}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{d\times 3}\\
\mathbf{0}_{3\times d}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{3\times 3}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Boyan’s chain tasks and experiment setup</h3>

<figure id="A6.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Hyperparameters for Boyan’s chain experiments in Section <span id="A6.T1.3" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S8" title="8 Experiments ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></span>.</figcaption>
<table id="A6.T1.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A6.T1.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">MRP (Boyan chain) states <math id="A6.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">feature dimension <math id="A6.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">discount factor <math id="A6.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">context length <math id="A6.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">rollout segment length <math id="A6.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1=11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1=11</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">query feature</td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{q}=x_{t+n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{q}=x_{t+n}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">softmax temperature <math id="A6.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">diagonal mixing <math id="A6.T1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">optimizer</td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Adam <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma and Ba, 2015</a>)</cite></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">learning rate</td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">weight decay</td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">batch size (contexts)</td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">mini-batches per epoch</td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">epochs</td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3000</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">number of layers <math id="A6.T1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.T1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T1.4.16" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T1.4.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">number of random seeds</td>
<td id="A6.T1.4.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><math id="A6.T1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07333v1/boyan.svg" id="A6.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:248/75;" width="248" height="75"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Boyan’s chain topology with nonzero transitions. Adapted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2025a)</a></cite>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task distribution.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2025a)</a></cite>, we use a randomized variant of Boyan’s chain <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boyan, 1999</a>)</cite> as an evaluation-task distribution.
Each call to the generator samples an ergodic MRP together with a randomized state representation
<math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x:\mathcal{S}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x:\mathcal{S}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and a ground-truth value function <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that is linear in <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The generation procedure is summarized in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Task distribution. ‣ F.3 Boyan’s chain tasks and experiment setup ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Boyan Chain MRP and Feature Generation (Adapted from Algorithm 3 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2025a)</a></cite>)</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> state space size <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\absolutevalue{\fS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\absolutevalue{\fS}</annotation></semantics></math>, feature dimension <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, discount factor <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{*}\sim\mathrm{Uniform}\quantity[(-1,1)^d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{*}\sim\mathrm{Uniform}\quantity[(-1,1)^d]</annotation></semantics></math>  // ground-truth weight

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(s)\sim\mathrm{Uniform}\quantity[(-1,1)^d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(s)\sim\mathrm{Uniform}\quantity[(-1,1)^d]</annotation></semantics></math>  // feature

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}(s)\leftarrow\langle w_{*},x(s)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}(s)\leftarrow\langle w_{*},x(s)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>  // ground-truth value function

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}\sim\mathrm{Uniform}\quantity[(0,1)^m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}\sim\mathrm{Uniform}\quantity[(0,1)^m]</annotation></semantics></math>   // initial distribution

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}\leftarrow p_{0}/\sum_{s}p_{0}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}\leftarrow p_{0}/\sum_{s}p_{0}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leftarrow 0_{m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leftarrow 0_{m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>   // transition function

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-2</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim\mathrm{Uniform}[(0,1)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim\mathrm{Uniform}[(0,1)]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(i,i+1)\leftarrow\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(i,i+1)\leftarrow\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(i,i+2)\leftarrow 1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(i,i+2)\leftarrow 1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg2.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(m-1,m)\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(m-1,m)\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\sim\mathrm{Uniform}\big[(0,1)^{m}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\sim\mathrm{Uniform}\big[(0,1)^{m}\big]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\leftarrow z/\sum_{s}z(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\leftarrow z/\sum_{s}z(s)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(m,1:m)\leftarrow z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(m,1:m)\leftarrow z</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leftarrow(I_{m}-\gamma p)v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leftarrow(I_{m}-\gamma p)v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>  // reward function

</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
                
                
               Define rewards by Bellman consistency: <math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leftarrow(I-\gamma P)v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leftarrow(I-\gamma P)v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg2.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> MRP <math id="alg2.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{0},p,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{0},p,r)</annotation></semantics></math> and feature map <math id="alg2.l21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training pipeline.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise stated, we set the context length <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=10</annotation></semantics></math>, feature dimension <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=4</annotation></semantics></math>, and discount factor <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>.
At the beginning of each epoch, we reset the MRP by sampling a fresh task (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Task distribution. ‣ F.3 Boyan’s chain tasks and experiment setup ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>),
roll out a single on-policy trajectory, and form overlapping length-<math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> contexts by sliding a window along the trajectory.
We train a single-head softmax ICTD block with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=3</annotation></semantics></math> layers under the minimal sparse parameterization
(Appendix <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Minimal Sparse Parameterization ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>).
Unless otherwise stated, we train for <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3000</annotation></semantics></math> epochs with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> mini-batches per epoch and a mini-batch size of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math> contexts.
Each experiment is repeated with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> random seeds and we aggregate results across seeds.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hyperparameters.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ F.3 Boyan’s chain tasks and experiment setup ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes the default hyperparameters used in Boyan’s chain experiments in Section <span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S8" title="8 Experiments ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Plotting details for Figures <span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S8.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Setup. ‣ 8 Experiments ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span>.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each random seed, we generate <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{MRP}}=3000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>MRP</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{MRP}}=3000</annotation></semantics></math> independent MRPs for evaluation and record diagnostics on them. Each evaluated point includes <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S8.E34" title="In Kernel diagonality. ‣ 8 Experiments ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) and related quantities computed from the same evaluation rollouts.
Emergence scores <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{em}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{em}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{em}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{em}}</annotation></semantics></math> are computed once per training step from the learned <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{0},A_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{0},A_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Figure <span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S8.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Setup. ‣ 8 Experiments ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span>(a).</span>
We select the best checkpoint as the training step that maximizes
<math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(V_{\mathrm{em}},A_{\mathrm{em}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(V_{\mathrm{em}},A_{\mathrm{em}})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., where both <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> emergence
are simultaneously high. At this checkpoint, we save the learned matrices
<math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#A6.E105" title="In Mask on 𝑉. ‣ F.2 Minimal Sparse Parameterization ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">105</span></a>) and (<a href="#A6.E107" title="In Mask on 𝐴. ‣ F.2 Minimal Sparse Parameterization ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">107</span></a>).
For visualization, each heatmap is normalized by its maximum absolute value and
rendered with a colormap over the range <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Figure <span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S8.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Setup. ‣ 8 Experiments ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span>(b).</span>
We bin evaluated points by <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> equal-width bins.
Within each bin, we plot the mean emergence scores <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{em}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{em}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{em}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{em}}</annotation></semantics></math> separately.
Shaded regions correspond to the interquartile range (25th-75th percentile) across random seeds.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Emergence vs. training step.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each seed, we smooth the per-step traces of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{em}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{em}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{em}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{em}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with a trailing average of window <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then truncate the curves at the seed-wise early-stop step that maximizes <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(V_{\mathrm{em}},A_{\mathrm{em}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(V_{\mathrm{em}},A_{\mathrm{em}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, we plot the mean <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> one s.e.m. across seeds (top: <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{em}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{em}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{em}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>em</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{em}}</annotation></semantics></math>; bottom: <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Figure <span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#A6.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Emergence vs. training step. ‣ F.3 Boyan’s chain tasks and experiment setup ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></span> shows that under the default hyperparameters in Table <span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"><a href="#A6.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ F.3 Boyan’s chain tasks and experiment setup ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>, the model automatically learns increasingly diagonal kernels (high <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) over training.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07333v1/emerVSsteps0p0.png" id="A6.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:286/238;" width="286" height="238" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Emergence vs. training steps under the default mask and <math id="A6.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Compute resources.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments were run on a single NVIDIA H100 GPU. The main experiments reported in Figure <span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S8.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Setup. ‣ 8 Experiments ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span> take approximately one hour of wall-clock time in total.
The appendix ablations, including the mask-relaxation experiments in Figure <span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"><a href="#A6.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ F.4.2 A-emergence score. ‣ F.4 Emergence metrics ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></span>, use the same single-H100 setup and account for the majority of the remaining compute.
The numerical verification experiments in Figure <span id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text"><a href="#A6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ F.6 Numerical verification on Theorem ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></span> are lightweight.
Across all reported experiments in the paper, the total compute is below 10 H100 GPU-hours.
Preliminary and debugging runs used comparable compute and did not substantially exceed this reported experimental budget.
The experiments use only synthetic Boyan-chain data, and the storage requirement is negligible.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.4 </span>Emergence metrics</h3>

<div id="A6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We quantify how closely the first softmax ICTD layer matches the ideal TD update
using two scalar scores <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{em},t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>em</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{em},t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{em},t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>em</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{em},t}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
A score of <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the ideal TD block.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.4.1 </span>V-emergence score.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At training step <math id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, let
<math id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(p_{r,t},p_{\gamma v^{\prime},t},p_{v,t})\doteq(V_{0,t})_{d+3,d{:}d+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≐</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{r,t},p_{\gamma v^{\prime},t},p_{v,t})\doteq(V_{0,t})_{d+3,d{:}d+3}</annotation></semantics></math>
denote the three coefficients that the first layer applies to the reward <math id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>,
bootstrap value <math id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma v^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma v^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and current value <math id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in its value update.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sign check.</span>
We enforce the TD sign pattern via</p>
<table id="A6.E109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}_{V,t}\doteq\mathbb{I}\bigl\{p_{r,t}&gt;0,\;p_{\gamma v^{\prime},t}&gt;0,\;p_{v,t}&lt;0\bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}_{V,t}\doteq\mathbb{I}\bigl\{p_{r,t}&gt;0,\;p_{\gamma v^{\prime},t}&gt;0,\;p_{v,t}&lt;0\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparability.</span>
We encourage comparable magnitudes.
Let</p>
<table id="A6.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{V,t}\doteq\frac{|p_{r,t}|+|p_{\gamma v^{\prime},t}|+|p_{v,t}|}{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{V,t}\doteq\frac{|p_{r,t}|+|p_{\gamma v^{\prime},t}|+|p_{v,t}|}{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We define the magnitude-ratio score</p>
<table id="A6.E110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{V,t}\doteq\max\Biggl\{0,\;1-\frac{\bigl||p_{r,t}|-m_{V,t}\bigr|+\bigl||p_{\gamma v^{\prime},t}|-m_{V,t}\bigr|+\bigl||p_{v,t}|-m_{V,t}\bigr|}{3\max\{m_{V,t},\varepsilon\}}\Biggr\}\in[0,1]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{V,t}\doteq\max\Biggl\{0,\;1-\frac{\bigl||p_{r,t}|-m_{V,t}\bigr|+\bigl||p_{\gamma v^{\prime},t}|-m_{V,t}\bigr|+\bigl||p_{v,t}|-m_{V,t}\bigr|}{3\max\{m_{V,t},\varepsilon\}}\Biggr\}\in[0,1],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a small constant.
This score is maximized when the three coefficients have the same magnitude. When <math id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{V,t}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{V,t}=0</annotation></semantics></math>
the definition yields <math id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{V,t}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{V,t}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The V-emergence score at step <math id="A6.SS4.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A6.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{em},t}\doteq\mathbb{I}_{V,t}\,C_{V,t}\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>em</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{em},t}\doteq\mathbb{I}_{V,t}\,C_{V,t}\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.4.2 </span>A-emergence score.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}}\doteq(A_{0,t})_{0{:}d,\,0{:}d}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>feat</mi></msubsup><mo>≐</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}}\doteq(A_{0,t})_{0{:}d,\,0{:}d}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> at training step <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
For diagnostics we work with a column-normalized nonnegative version.
For <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A6.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\widehat{A}_{t})[:,j]\doteq\begin{cases}\frac{\bigl|(A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}})[:,j]\bigr|}{\|(A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}})[:,j]\|_{2}}&amp;\|(A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}})[:,j]\|_{2}&gt;0,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>feat</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>feat</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>feat</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{A}_{t})[:,j]\doteq\begin{cases}\frac{\bigl|(A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}})[:,j]\bigr|}{\|(A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}})[:,j]\|_{2}}&amp;\|(A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}})[:,j]\|_{2}&gt;0,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">that is, we divide each column by its <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm and take absolute values.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diagonality.</span>
From <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> we measure how much of the <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> mass lies on the diagonal via</p>
<table id="A6.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{diag},t}\doteq\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{d}(\widehat{A}_{t})_{ii}}{\max\Bigl\{\sum_{i,j=1}^{d}(\widehat{A}_{t})[i,j],\,\varepsilon\Bigr\}}\in[0,1]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{diag},t}\doteq\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{d}(\widehat{A}_{t})_{ii}}{\max\Bigl\{\sum_{i,j=1}^{d}(\widehat{A}_{t})[i,j],\,\varepsilon\Bigr\}}\in[0,1],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a small constant.
This quantity is close to <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is nearly diagonal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparability.</span>
Let <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\doteq\mathrm{diag}(A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>feat</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\doteq\mathrm{diag}(A_{0,t}^{\mathrm{feat}})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We encourage the diagonal entries to be comparable in magnitude.
Let</p>
<table id="A6.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{A,t}\doteq\frac{1}{d}\sum_{i=1}^{d}(a_{t})_{i},\qquad C_{A,t}\doteq\max\Biggl\{0,\;1-\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{d}|(a_{t})_{i}-m_{A,t}|}{d\,\max\{m_{A,t},\varepsilon\}}\Biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{A,t}\doteq\frac{1}{d}\sum_{i=1}^{d}(a_{t})_{i},\qquad C_{A,t}\doteq\max\Biggl\{0,\;1-\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{d}|(a_{t})_{i}-m_{A,t}|}{d\,\max\{m_{A,t},\varepsilon\}}\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By construction, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{A,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{A,t}</annotation></semantics></math> measures whether the raw diagonal entries
are close to a common value, but it does not separately enforce that
this common value is positive.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The A-emergence score at step <math id="A6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A6.E111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{em},t}\doteq A_{\mathrm{diag},t}\cdot C_{A,t}\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>em</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{em},t}\doteq A_{\mathrm{diag},t}\cdot C_{A,t}\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A6.F6.2" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07333v1/training_metrics_avg.svg" id="A6.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:229/191;" width="229" height="191"></object>
