</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A6.F6.3" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07333v1/x1.svg" id="A6.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:229/191;" width="229" height="191"></object>
<p id="A6.F6.3.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A6.F6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b) Relaxed-mask: training trajectories.</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A6.F6.4" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07333v1/P_S_vs_diag_avg.svg" id="A6.F6.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/153;" width="229" height="153"></object>
<p id="A6.F6.4.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A6.F6.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c) Full-mask: emergence vs. <math id="A6.F6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A6.F6.5" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07333v1/x2.svg" id="A6.F6.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/153;" width="229" height="153"></object>
<p id="A6.F6.5.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A6.F6.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(d) Relaxed-mask: emergence vs. <math id="A6.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A6.F6.6" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><img src="2605.07333v1/x3.png" id="A6.F6.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/115;" width="229" height="115" alt="Refer to caption">
<p id="A6.F6.6.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A6.F6.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(e) Full-mask: mean <math id="A6.F6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> at best joint emergence.</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A6.F6.7" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><img src="2605.07333v1/x4.png" id="A6.F6.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/115;" width="229" height="115" alt="Refer to caption">
<p id="A6.F6.7.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A6.F6.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(f) Relaxed-mask: mean <math id="A6.F6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> at best joint emergence.</span></p>
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Mask relaxation on Boyan’s chain.
We compare the full-mask setting in (<a href="#A6.E108" title="In Mask on 𝐴. ‣ F.2 Minimal Sparse Parameterization ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">108</span></a>) (left column) and the relaxed-mask setting (<a href="#A6.E112" title="In F.5 Mask Relaxation ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">112</span></a>) (right column).
All plots are averaged and visualized in the same way as in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Boyan’s chain tasks and experiment setup ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>,
using <math id="A6.F6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> random seeds over <math id="A6.F6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9000</annotation></semantics></math> training steps.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.5 </span>Mask Relaxation</h3>

<div id="A6.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We next study how emergence depends on the strength of the structural masking constraint in <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on the Boyan task
distribution.
All experiments in this subsection use the same Boyan training
setup as in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Boyan’s chain tasks and experiment setup ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>, except that we apply the linearly
annealed diagonal mixing coefficient <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A6.E104" title="In F.1 Multi-task TD ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">104</span></a>), increasing it from <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.68" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.68</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.68</annotation></semantics></math>
to <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.80</annotation></semantics></math> over the first <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8000</annotation></semantics></math> steps and then holding it fixed at <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.80</annotation></semantics></math>.
It is trained for <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9000</annotation></semantics></math> gradient steps in total (corresponding to <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="900" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>900</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">900</annotation></semantics></math> MRPs per seed in our implementation).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce the diagonal mixing coefficient <math id="A6.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> purely as a training-speed heuristic for this ablation:
under the default setting in Section <span id="A6.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#S8" title="8 Experiments ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></span>, kernel diagonality emerges without any auxiliary bias given sufficient training,
whereas here we use <math id="A6.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> to accelerate convergence so that the mask-relaxation comparison can be run with a smaller training budget
without changing the qualitative emergence behavior.
Throughout, we keep <math id="A6.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{mask}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>mask</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{mask}}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We compare two masking configurations for <math id="A6.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. The full-mask setting uses the
default <math id="A6.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{mask}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>mask</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{mask}}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A6.E108" title="In Mask on 𝐴. ‣ F.2 Minimal Sparse Parameterization ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">108</span></a>).
In the
relaxed-mask setting, we change it to</p>
<table id="A6.E112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{mask}}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbbm{1}_{d\times d}&amp;\mathbbm{1}_{d\times 3}\\
\mathbbm{1}_{3\times d}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{3\times 3}\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>mask</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{mask}}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbbm{1}_{d\times d}&amp;\mathbbm{1}_{d\times 3}\\
\mathbbm{1}_{3\times d}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{3\times 3}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(112)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A6.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ F.4.2 A-emergence score. ‣ F.4 Emergence metrics ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> summarizes the results and shows relaxing the mask preserves the emergence behavior.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.6 </span>Numerical verification on Theorem <span id="A6.SS6.2" class="ltx_text"><a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="A6.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We verified Theorem <span id="A6.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span> experimentally. For each trial we sample a fresh prompt <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(n+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+3)\times(n+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and run the depth-<math id="A6.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>
forward recursion of a single-head block.
In parallel, we unroll the reference softmax ICTD recursion from Theorem <span id="A6.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"><a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ Target-value head. ‣ 3 Transformers Can Implement In-Context Weighted Softmax TD ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span> on the same context,
producing <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{l}^{(n+1)}\}_{l=0}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{l}^{(n+1)}\}_{l=0}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> for the query prediction.
We report the layer-wise log discrepancy</p>
<table id="A6.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{l}\;\doteq\;\log\bigl|v_{l}(S_{n})-y_{l}^{(n+1)}\bigr|,\qquad v_{l}(S_{n})\;=\;Z_{l}[d+3,n+1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≐</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{l}\;\doteq\;\log\bigl|v_{l}(S_{n})-y_{l}^{(n+1)}\bigr|,\qquad v_{l}(S_{n})\;=\;Z_{l}[d+3,n+1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=8</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=20</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=10</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{l}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{l}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and repeat over <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> trials in double precision.
We test masked-softmax, ReLU, ELU<math id="A6.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and an RBF kernelization for <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Figure <a href="#A6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ F.6 Numerical verification on Theorem ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Details ‣ Beyond Linear Attention: Softmax Transformers Implement In-Context Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows that <math id="A6.SS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> stays at numerical precision across depth,
confirming that the residual update realizes a one-step nonlinear in-context TD update.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07333v1/log_error_nonlinear.svg" id="A6.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/140;" width="286" height="140"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Kernel weighted TD verification. Layer-wise log discrepancy <math id="A6.F7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> under different kernelizations <math id="A6.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
